9EyblVwuXvQ01A_2_2">3,167,357</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:84.82%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">One to five years</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.63%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">&#160;</b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.53%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_11_30_2025_ifrs-full_MaturityAxis_ifrs-full_LaterThanOneYearAndNotLaterThanFiveYearsMember_OBFsrJ8X50eEH5LdOTsoww" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:UndiscountedOperatingLeasePayments" scale="0" id="Tc_eC7gFKTEKkG2o0NPVbH8gg_3_2">7,097,383</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:84.82%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.63%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">&#160;</b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.53%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_11_30_2025_jwmPbnqljEWY3xAvOg0B8w" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:UndiscountedOperatingLeasePayments" scale="0" id="Tc_WSw6P1s9IUaCtfvep_I_bw_4_2">10,264,740</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Included in rent expense for the three-month and nine-month periods ended May 31, 2026 were $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_3_1_2026_To_5_31_2026_HRfrjIJ0P0K6ZjEBCcZDuw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ExpenseRelatingToShorttermLeasesForWhichRecognitionExemptionHasBeenUsed" scale="0" id="Narr_17-iVuFafEChjpJdSUguWQ">328,167</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ExpenseRelatingToShorttermLeasesForWhichRecognitionExemptionHasBeenUsed" scale="0" id="Narr_t8ATxQP5_kCoGbx-HjaoDA">987,555</ix:nonFraction> respectively of short-term lease expense [May 31, 2025 &#8211; $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_3_1_2025_To_5_31_2025_YzDrR-cm1ESskPmPNnYYWA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ExpenseRelatingToShorttermLeasesForWhichRecognitionExemptionHasBeenUsed" scale="0" id="Narr_tqywj08Jjk2V-2k6bw1xVA">108,954</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2024_To_5_31_2025_tPSEQK3-e0Ggkh2iXORvFw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ExpenseRelatingToShorttermLeasesForWhichRecognitionExemptionHasBeenUsed" scale="0" id="Narr_BI51dJ7D3UOiTa504_cvVg">331,360</ix:nonFraction> respectively]. As at May 31, 2026, the lease liabilities have a weighted average interest rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_DJ_Gbs_XZ0-yoXCWW_X2kQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:WeightedAverageLesseesIncrementalBorrowingRateAppliedToLeaseLiabilitiesRecognisedAtDateOfInitialApplicationOfIFRS16" scale="-2" id="Narr_PlWOA9l5xkWmXtu7NmQR2Q">8.21</ix:nonFraction>% [August 31, 2025 <span style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';">&#8211;</span> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_8_31_2025_HfFgBoy0ZEu9yU3FcK5xig" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:WeightedAverageLesseesIncrementalBorrowingRateAppliedToLeaseLiabilitiesRecognisedAtDateOfInitialApplicationOfIFRS16" scale="-2" id="Narr_piktsJqdgE23j04Qn3IT2w">7.93</ix:nonFraction>%).</p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" name="vmar:DisclosureOfFloorPlanFinancingTextBlock" id="Tb_qJQYwz2kiE2xrVYDc-6jfQ" continuedAt="Tb_qJQYwz2kiE2xrVYDc-6jfQ_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">14. Floor plan financing</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Company finances most of its new and certain of its used boat inventory through standardized floor plan facilities with either various financial institutions and manufacturer-affiliated finance companies or directly with individual manufacturer-affiliated finance companies and other lending institutions. The new and used boat floor plan facilities bear interest at variable rates based on either SOFR or prime rates, depending on the lender arrangement. The weighted average interest rate on floor plan facilities was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_8_31_2025_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingMember_ifrs-full_RangeAxis_srt_WeightedAverageMember_K0tSyl6jtkK7ZsME_FWmgQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:BorrowingsInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_WrfaV9pJPU-I6M0TbFPPEw">9.7</ix:nonFraction>% as of August 31, 2025. The new and used boat floor plan facilities are collateralized by boat inventory and other assets. The vehicle floor plan facilities </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">10</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;">Vision Marine Technologies Inc.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes to the condensed interim consolidated financial statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">(Unaudited)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">May 31, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_CZnMXr5o3Uy7Qfey21GXyw_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_URCzFbc09UCYb5Syp4Y6FQ_1_4"></a><a id="Tc_m2YD5vHdU0KR3uY13NVqVg_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_Ki0dMF3pbku-ybE9GK7CWA_2_4"></a><a id="Tc_fXwjzAXjRUiXgmgTJla1-g_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_GNqovAqqNEqXo6_kIiTyUQ_3_4"></a><a id="Tc_G-Dl_ApMpkKTMWwBxPNjXg_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_D_58QU8-jkaiMUv7krOujQ_4_4"></a><a id="Tc_yMBWK1T30Eu6W95WSxn8RA_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_C0TNCrtvWUOmIszWwkZi2w_5_4"></a><a id="Tc_0YoSg34J5U2rYsVxkvTQMQ_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_dqgI0kv44Uqbodw7I22RBg_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_0xvL7MxPP0KmoylP2O3yGg_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_Ryt9Xq6fTUuWBivQjiTlUg_8_2"></a><a id="Tc_aAhpoIcd5kO2VX4VdKzssw_9_0"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_qJQYwz2kiE2xrVYDc-6jfQ_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">contain a number of covenants, including, among others, covenants restricting the Company with respect to the creation of liens and changes in ownership, officers and key management personnel. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;">Prior to the </span>Company<span style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';">&#8217;</span>s acquisition of NVG<span style="font-size:10pt;">, NVG had not been compliant with all covenants of its floor plan and mortgage lenders due to the change of ownership when NVG purchased </span><span style="font-size:10pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2022_To_8_31_2023_dei_LegalEntityAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_vmar_IfrsMajorityShareholderMember_ZsPx1MYEyk2FVR7svx2wew" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:ProportionOfOwnershipInterestAcquired" scale="-2" id="Narr_LXuubZnwcUOI5RUp0Db-Mw">86</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:10pt;"> of the shares held by a founding shareholder in 2023 as well as the change of ownership that has occurred with acquisition of </span><span style="font-size:10pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_8_31_2023_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ZoLNYrSxJUejk09DDjwhlA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:PercentageOfVotingEquityInterestsAcquired" scale="-2" id="Narr_r-gSwST4zkismsrAY3rwzA">100</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:10pt;"> of NVG by the Company. In addition, NVG had not been compliant with the covenant requiring threshold Debt Service Coverage Ratios due to the reduced margins throughout 2024 caused by excessive dealer inventory levels, fierce competition and high floor plan interest triggering technical defaults with </span><span style="font-size:10pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_Lender_M5M39kwRj0G6nY-CGL0QVA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingMember_S7RpzbjUJE2q_C0V_JlefQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="vmar:NumberOfLenders" scale="0" id="Narr_h2RKPkPpy0OL9SUG_9LZqQ">five</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:10pt;"> of its lenders, namely:</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Wells Fargo Commercial Finance</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Bank of Montreal (BMO)</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Valley National Bank</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Shore Premier/Centennial Bank</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Northpoint Commercial Finance</span></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">At the Acquisition Date, all of the above lenders, except for Wells Fargo Commercial Finance, had consented to the change of ownership and signed forbearance agreements as the Company regains profitability and updates documentation with all lenders post-acquisition. The floor plan owed to Wells Fargo Commercial Finance in the amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_vmar_WellsFargoCommercialFinanceMember_VLWuk6nvxEaYuHnNN8O9AA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:NotionalAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_FmnH91709EiVEMHubEN08A">1,907,751</ix:nonFraction> was assumed by one of the Company&#8217;s suppliers, Beneteau Group. The Company remains in good standing with all of its current floor plan lenders at May 31, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">During the nine-month period ended May 31, 2026, the Company entered into a floor plan financing arrangement with Yamaha Motor Finance Corporation (&#8220;Yamaha&#8221;), providing for a revolving credit facility of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithYamahaMotorFinanceCorporationMember_mJCvZhe8MEOKIKzt9DGD6g" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsLineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="0" id="Narr_ELtOUZqLp0eeB8_HU_CoZw">300,000</ix:nonFraction>. In connection with this facility, the Company obtained an ILOC of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithYamahaMotorFinanceCorporationMember_3DfuCZ1V6UWnKnTMNEs1Zw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ProceedsFromCurrentBorrowings" scale="0" id="Narr_Kar5RWi5CUueaUCccYPR5w">150,000</ix:nonFraction> issued by its banking partner in favor of Yamaha <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 25]</i>. The ILOC is secured by restricted cash of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithYamahaMotorFinanceCorporationMember_mJCvZhe8MEOKIKzt9DGD6g" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:RestrictedCashAndCashEquivalents" scale="0" id="Narr_lP2CrmcSJkiDFvHqeqKnFg">150,000</ix:nonFraction> <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 5]</i>, which is held in a segregated account and is not available for general operating purposes. The requirement to maintain restricted cash reduces the Company&#8217;s available liquidity. Management continues to monitor its liquidity position and compliance with financing arrangements on an ongoing basis.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">During the nine-month period ended May 31, 2026, the Company entered into a floor plan financing arrangement with Shore Premier Finance, a division of Centennial Bank (&#8220;Shore Premier&#8221;), providing for a revolving credit facility of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithShorePremierFinanceMember_LIm8z5yyC0mmQT62db5ZDw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsLineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="0" id="Narr_OjTZW5SGOkeyL2dnGib_CQ">4,000,000</ix:nonFraction>. In connection with this facility, the Company obtained ILOCs of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithShorePremierFinanceMember_Hlfk9Qj2MUatCw_s3xlC9g" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ProceedsFromCurrentBorrowings" scale="0" id="Narr_D2PyZfk46kKUF4VvK_6XHg">200,000</ix:nonFraction> issued by its banking partner in favor of Shore Premier <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 25]</i>. The ILOC is secured by restricted cash of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithShorePremierFinanceMember_LIm8z5yyC0mmQT62db5ZDw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:RestrictedCashAndCashEquivalents" scale="0" id="Narr_egtSf-II-0O989IDDjNFig">200,000</ix:nonFraction> <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 5]</i>, which is held in a segregated account and is not available for general operating purposes. The requirement to maintain restricted cash reduces the Company&#8217;s available liquidity. Management continues to monitor its liquidity position and compliance with financing arrangements on an ongoing basis.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The table below summarizes the movement in the floor plan financing during the nine-month period ended May 31, 2026 and the fiscal year ended August 31, 2025:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" name="vmar:FloorPlanFinancingRollForwardTableTextBlock" id="Tb_f7C5neYsSUST6NjF4HdKFA" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:68.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.76%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:13.14%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.75%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:13.13%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:68.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.76%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">&#160;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;</b></p></td><td sty