rredSharesMember_Tm_lhkbCKU2yINq4JBd9jw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:GainLossRelatedToValuationOfDerivativeFinancialInstruments" scale="0" id="Narr_wqgJXSyFxE6qheCT61OENA">2,297</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_ifrs-full_DerivativesMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfShareCapitalAxis_vmar_SeriesBConvertiblePreferredSharesMember_nFkfN4HH7UW1OM25kgIu5Q" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:GainLossRelatedToValuationOfDerivativeFinancialInstruments" scale="0" id="Narr_mtmh2yb5sUmqMXP7C3gOEQ">664</ix:nonFraction> respectively [May 31, 2025 &#8211; loss of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_3_1_2025_To_5_31_2025_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_ifrs-full_DerivativesMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfShareCapitalAxis_vmar_SeriesBConvertiblePreferredSharesMember_nmb0AIiAVkWLHuojCl6UaQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:GainLossRelatedToValuationOfDerivativeFinancialInstruments" sign="-" scale="0" id="Narr_aRprrETFT0u-kHWKKggH-Q">9,447</ix:nonFraction> and a gain of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2024_To_5_31_2025_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_ifrs-full_DerivativesMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfShareCapitalAxis_vmar_SeriesBConvertiblePreferredSharesMember_MTMefgQn4kWPMOYT-0ekyw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:GainLossRelatedToValuationOfDerivativeFinancialInstruments" scale="0" id="Narr_Fq08aN_bR0OktroMwo5xuQ">892,239</ix:nonFraction> respectively], related to the valuation of these instruments in net finance expense (income) <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 21]</i>. Included in this gain is the accelerated amortization of the deferred loss at issuance. The portion of this balance that was applicable to the Series B Convertible Preferred Shares was written off completely at November 30, 2024 because the amount of the deferred loss balance at that date exceeded the fair value attributable to these instruments at that date. As such, the Company recorded an accelerated loss of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_ifrs-full_DerivativesMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfShareCapitalAxis_vmar_SeriesBConvertiblePreferredSharesMember_nFkfN4HH7UW1OM25kgIu5Q" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="vmar:AmortizationOfDeferredLossDerivativeFinancialLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_GROyEXmSRUOOAkBG_LiQ1Q">nil</ix:nonFraction> on these instruments for the nine-month period ended May 31, 2026 [May 31, 2025 &#8211; $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2024_To_5_31_2025_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_ifrs-full_DerivativesMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfShareCapitalAxis_vmar_SeriesBConvertiblePreferredSharesMember_MTMefgQn4kWPMOYT-0ekyw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:AmortizationOfDeferredLossDerivativeFinancialLiabilities" sign="-" scale="0" id="Narr_n0exuJvUukKEwJVZDYtZMw">580,881</ix:nonFraction>].</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Purchase consideration &#8211; NVG acquisition</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As part of the NVG acquisition <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 4]</i>, the Company entered into the following financial instruments:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Initial Convertible Note is a convertible promissory note which was issued to Roger Moore, a related party </span><i style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">[note 17]</i><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">, on June 20, 2025 for </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_InitialConvertibleNoteMember_eSMsbrkPUUK976dqQPtghQ" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:NotionalAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_rt-O5DGDCEmeG0m3q2xu0w">4</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> million, with a maturity date of June 20, 2027. The convertible note accrues interest at </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_InitialConvertibleNoteMember_eSMsbrkPUUK976dqQPtghQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:BorrowingsInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_Df6CDc75IE2VltGYAx2N3w">6.0</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> per annum and has monthly interest payments of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_6_20_2025_To_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_InitialConvertibleNoteMember_iDxRHVCudU2lNRU7l5pkng" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentPeriodicPaymentInterest" scale="0" id="Narr_hfqXA5OBjEuFeeX8ZtxZlg">20,000</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The convertible note can be converted at anytime to Voting Common Shares of the Company at an exercise price of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ggFZRiqKa0a4KEAPuuMx5Q" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_InitialConvertibleNoteMember_eSMsbrkPUUK976dqQPtghQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice" scale="0" id="Narr_zFU7UvomhEGltrOY89Yt2A">3,449.60</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">.</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Subsequent Convertible Note is a convertible promissory note which is expected to be issued to Roger Moore, a related party </span><i style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">[note 17]</i><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">, for </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_10a88UVXBU2QcbxRYL11ow" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:NotionalAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_DWv15aGXq0quIJcY0IIW_w">2</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> million with a term of </span><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_6_20_2025_To_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_qyVma1QoUUShBlUgu2OI2Q" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentTerm" id="Narr_ohljtkZwX0Oe6owGB187bg"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">36 months</span></ix:nonNumeric><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The convertible note will accrue interest at </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_10a88UVXBU2QcbxRYL11ow" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:BorrowingsInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_Hh0PwB4QxUCM4SeRnATb4w">6.0</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> per annum and have monthly interest payments of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_6_20_2025_To_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_qyVma1QoUUShBlUgu2OI2Q" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentPeriodicPaymentInterest" scale="0" id="Narr_DcmG1ejb8keN4PEkHoLZ8A">10,000</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The convertible note will be convertible at anytime to Voting Common Shares of the Company at an exercise price of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ggFZRiqKa0a4KEAPuuMx5Q" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_10a88UVXBU2QcbxRYL11ow" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice" scale="0" id="Narr_T383BrL-p0G0Z_aaDndGCA">3,449.60</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The issuance is contingent on the outcome of certain legal claims against NVG. A </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_ifrs-full_UnobservableInputsAxis_vmar_ProbabilityOfIssuanceMeasurementInputMember_jNjnC0MvkUmmWlovIwtbdg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:SignificantUnobservableInputLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_47RgawN1mEOCdyfHjVCxOw">50</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> probability was assigned to the issuance of this instrument.</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Real Estate Note is a convertible promissory note which was issued to Roger Moore, a related party </span><i style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">[note 16]</i><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">, on October 21, 2025 following completion of certain real estate transactions </span><i style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">[note 17]</i><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">, for </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_10_21_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_RealEstateNoteMember_C7zawAdt806XnrPkFzdPvQ" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:NotionalAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_eNq8eK6ecU-TjavuH9DlGw">2</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> million with a term of </span><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_10_21_2025_To_10_21_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_RealEstateNoteMember_xx00duWy3Ui-xPCQYTE7Dg" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentTerm" id="Narr_ArRxWh-8akufj6s_BN07UQ"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">36 months</span></ix:nonNumeric><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The convertible note accrues interest at </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_10_21_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_RealEstateNoteMember_C7zawAdt806XnrPkFzdPvQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:BorrowingsInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_W1BDX-Itx0adyeIRIsaEvw">6.0</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> per annum and has monthly interest payments of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_10_21_2025_To_10_21_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_RealEstateNoteMember_xx00duWy3Ui-xPCQYTE7Dg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentPeriodicPaymentInterest" scale="0" id="Narr__Y0d7N4cUk-3G5KE5MeKKQ">10,000</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The convertible note will be convertible at anytime to Voting Common Shares of the Company at an exercise price of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ggFZRiqKa0a4KEAPuuMx5Q" contextRef="As_Of_10_21_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_RealEstateNoteMember_C7zawAdt806XnrPkFzdPvQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsDebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice" scale="0" id="Narr_avL4PsxKAkSU5x_xlA8mXQ">3,449.60</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">.</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Share Consideration consists of up to </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_PSKhk4L0BEuBjbMNWXfihw" contextRef="As_Of_10_21_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_CategoriesOfRelatedPartiesAxis_vmar_RogerMooreMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfShareCapitalAxis_vmar_VotingCommonStockMember_vJufyZ0s7kiJnkAaioLT5w" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:NumberOfInstrumentsOrInterestsIssuedOrIssuable" scale="0" id="Narr_U18nYuNQ8k-Dq61XfoTkug">638</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> Voting Common Shares of the Company to be issued to Roger Moore, a related party </span><i style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">[note 17]</i><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">. The issuance is contingent on the completion of certain real estate transactions </span><i style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">[note 17]</i><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">.</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Initial Convertible Note, the Subsequent Convertible Note and the Real Estate Note contain embedded conversion features which require bifurcation into debt and option components in accordance with IAS 32 and IFRS 9. On June 20, 2025, the acquisition date of NVG, the fair value of each component was determined in accordance with IFRS 13 using valuation techniques consistent with those applied by an independent valuation specialist.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">16</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;">Vision Marine Technologies Inc.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes to the condensed interim consolidated financial statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">(Unaudited)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">May 31, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="_c151e329_ee56_47c8_8f70_7a841626d99f"></a><a id="Tc_y--FXzPSPU658TfdZfJ_OA_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_qSkwavF-202pxIKk2PM7bw_1_4"></a><a id="Tc_2y73GiCE8UOzrUl4KP0TkA_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_HdRSNY7d3kmifuWQ6V2A9A_2_4"></a><a id="Tc_0Ro5swL5X0yV6fnhWN0KZA_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_wNo0AJYNnUWk-03TFm-KJw_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_xanmGE7500WwaG8z0C6_Ow_5_0"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_yhWaOf3I50yp7kPTGUjnxg_cont5" continuedAt="Tb_yhWaOf3I50yp7kPTGUjnxg_cont6"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The debt components were valued using a discounted cash flow model based on the contractual interest and principal payments, discounted using credit-adjusted market yields reflective of the Company&#8217;s estimated unsecured borrowing rate and observable credit spreads for CCC-rated U.S. Consumer Discretionary issuers with similar maturities. Where applicable, present-value adjustments were applied to instruments expected to be issued at a future date.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The conversion option components were valued using a Black-Scholes option pricing model, which incorporated Level 3 inputs including:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">the Company&#8217;s quoted share price on the valuation date;</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">expected volatility based on historical daily, weekly and monthly volatility observations for the Company and comparable issuers;</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">risk-free interest rates derived from U.S. Treasury yields with maturities matching each instrument&#8217;s expected life;</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">expected terms to maturity consistent with the contractual lives of each instrument (adjusted for expected issuance timing where relevant);</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">a </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_TypesOfFinancialLiabilitiesAxis_vmar_EmbeddedDerivativeMember_ifrs-full_UnobservableInputsAxis_vmar_DividendYieldMeasurementInputMember_ifrs-full_ValuationTechniquesUsedInFairValueMeasurementAxis_ifrs-full_OptionPricingModelMember_InyGNJhTu06g8kcehfjQ6w" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:SignificantUnobservableInputLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_LOZ0RfXC30-2ZzyTWkUK2g">0</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> dividend yield; and</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">for the Subsequent Convertible Note, a </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_SubsequentConvertibleNoteMember_ifrs-full_TypesOfFinancialLiabilitiesAxis_vmar_EmbeddedDerivativeMember_ifrs-full_UnobservableInputsAxis_vmar_ProbabilityOfIssuanceMeasurementInputMember_ifrs-full_ValuationTechniquesUsedInFairValueMeasurementAxis_ifrs-full_OptionPricingModelMember_SfrmPwSms0i7fy86MViZAQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:SignificantUnobservableInputLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_8KSE7XWQLkevJsg1OipygQ">50</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> probability weighting to reflect the contingent issuance conditions.</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The contingent Share Consideration was measured at the Company&#8217;s closing share price on June 20, 2025 of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ggFZRiqKa0a4KEAPuuMx5Q" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_TypesOfFinancialLiabilitiesAxis_ifrs-full_ContingentConsiderationMember_ifrs-full_UnobservableInputsAxis_vmar_DiscountForLackOfMarketabilityMeasurementInputMember_WoGlPc-SNES5LmKDX1zF-g" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsSharePrice" scale="0" id="Narr_E_-bHrsngEeEUJtNPkQKyg">3,136.00</ix:nonFraction>, adjusted for a discount for lack of marketability of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_TypesOfFinancialLiabilitiesAxis_ifrs-full_ContingentConsiderationMember_-ZfEnNAiKku_bFooZhKtXA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:SignificantUnobservableInputLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_T9IP2Gg0JUWcMna1PPfrdg">25</ix:nonFraction>%. As the Share Consideration meets the definition of an equity-settled instrument, it was recorded in Contributed Surplus.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In accordance with IFRS 9, each convertible note was assessed to determine whether the conversion option was closely related to the debt host. As the conversion features were not considered closely related, each note was bifurcated into (i) a long-term debt host measured at amortized cost and (ii) an embedded derivative measured at Fair Value Through Profit and Loss. In addition, the contingent share consideration was evaluated and classified as equity.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">At June 20, 2025, the embedded conversion options within the three notes were valued using a Black-Scholes option pricing model, taking into account expected volatility, risk-free rates, remaining terms, and the fixed conversion price. The corresponding debt hosts were measured using credit-adjusted market discount rates.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Given the variability associated with the various components of these instruments, they were recorded as debt hosts and derivative liabilities and will be subject to fair value adjustments at the issuance date and at subsequent balance sheet dates.</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" name="vmar:ScheduleOfAllocationOfDebtHostsAndEmbeddedDerivativesInFinancialInstrumentsTableTextBlock" id="Group_Sk_nPqnBYkCsiFQnmbtedw" continuedAt="Group_Sk_nPqnBYkCsiFQnmbtedw_2" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The allocation between debt hosts and embedded derivatives at June 20, 2025 is as follows:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:80%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:69.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.62%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.48%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:69.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;margin:0pt;">&#160;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.62%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Debt Host</b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;margin:0pt;">&#160;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.48%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Derivative Liability</b></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:69.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.62%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.48%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">$</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:69.18%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Initial Convertible Note</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.62%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_InitialConvertibleNoteMember_ifrs-full_TypesOfFinancialLiabilitiesAxis_vmar_DebtInstrumentHostMember_UczhBJhb1k6cHK-gBghOaw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:FinancialLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_BLdwTnmBu0-Xd1RAjwlP0w_3_2">3,282,369</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.48%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_6_20_2025_ifrs-full_BusinessCombinationsAxis_vmar_NauticalVenturesGroupIncMember_ifrs-full_ClassesOfFinancialInstrumentsAxis_vmar_InitialConvertibleNoteMember_ifrs-full_TypesOfFinancialLiabilitiesAxis_vmar_EmbeddedDerivativeMember_G3DCE9-VKkuSa92hKSIkXA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:FinancialLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_NckqR4XWikKY4FCg6j-_ww_3_4">2,319,565</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:69.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt