="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2024_To_5_31_2025_tPSEQK3-e0Ggkh2iXORvFw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:LeaseTermination" scale="0" id="Tc_7dApAMgU5UC_OqxflpBEWA_7_4">32,062</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:70.04%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Change in derivative liabilities due to partial settlements of convertible notes - related party</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.18%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.79%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:ChangeInDerivativeLiabilitiesDueToPartialSettlementsOfConvertibleNotesRelatedParty" scale="0" id="Tc_BVyaIspmWke3s3uhhsuyWQ_8_2">17,578</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.17%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.79%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> &#8212;</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:70.04%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Initial recognition of derivative liabilities</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.18%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.79%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:InitialRecognitionOfDerivativeLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc__OiCYl6Cs0ygSs8tZu8FPg_9_2">2,867,806</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.17%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.79%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2024_To_5_31_2025_tPSEQK3-e0Ggkh2iXORvFw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:InitialRecognitionOfDerivativeLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_EXnHvgQiB0GLuxfkmhFI5w_9_4">2,215,564</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:70.04%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Conversion of Series A Convertible Preferred Shares</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.18%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.79%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> &#8212;</b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.17%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"> <span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.79%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2024_To_5_31_2025_tPSEQK3-e0Ggkh2iXORvFw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:PreferredStockConvertibleValueOfSharesConverted" scale="0" id="Tc_2oQ8Y9AP00yaZQHv5aEj3A_10_4">308,692</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" name="ifrs-full:DisclosureOfCommitmentsExplanatory" id="Tb_ob40TqhLrEi2ItaLel-a4Q" continuedAt="Tb_ob40TqhLrEi2ItaLel-a4Q_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">25. Commitments and contingencies</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">ILOC</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In connection with its floor plan financing arrangement with Yamaha <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 14]</i>, the Company has provided credit support in the form of a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithYamahaMotorFinanceCorporationMember_3DfuCZ1V6UWnKnTMNEs1Zw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ProceedsFromCurrentBorrowings" scale="0" id="Narr_ezlo2J2OvkCeSIDB4OL71A">150,000</ix:nonFraction> ILOC issued by its banking partner. The ILOC supports a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithYamahaMotorFinanceCorporationMember_mJCvZhe8MEOKIKzt9DGD6g" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsLineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="0" id="Narr_-w0-H52nYUqDQbQRnac3aQ">300,000</ix:nonFraction> floor plan facility and may be drawn upon by Yamaha in the event of default by the Company under the related financing agreement. As at May 31, 2026, no amounts have been drawn under this arrangement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In connection with its floor plan financing arrangement with Shore Premier <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 14]</i>, the Company has provided credit support in the form of a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithShorePremierFinanceMember_Hlfk9Qj2MUatCw_s3xlC9g" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ProceedsFromCurrentBorrowings" scale="0" id="Narr_4kxPGljGKEau6jIdu35bCw">200,000</ix:nonFraction> ILOC issued by its banking partner. The ILOC supports a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_BorrowingsByNameAxis_vmar_FloorPlanFinancingWithShorePremierFinanceMember_LIm8z5yyC0mmQT62db5ZDw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsLineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="0" id="Narr_iOkMbk7Qo02fyEZBpB3_Ag">4,000,000</ix:nonFraction> floor plan facility and may be drawn upon by Shore Premier in the event of default by the Company under the related financing agreement. As at May 31, 2026, no amounts have been drawn under this arrangement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The standby letter of credit represents a contingent obligation and is accounted for in accordance with IAS 37. As the likelihood of a draw is not considered probable, no provision has been recognized in these interim condensed consolidated financial statements.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Battery supply agreement with Neogy SAS</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As previously disclosed, the Company had entered into a battery supply agreement with Neogy SAS (&#8220;Neogy&#8221;) providing for the purchase of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_jxoTQ30H-Ee41XEeUfi1tg" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:NumberOfBatteriesCommittedToBePurchased" scale="0" id="Narr_ZZMhAqGmAkWO6frJSUVgGw">192</ix:nonFraction> batteries. As at May 31, 2026, the Company had received <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_jxoTQ30H-Ee41XEeUfi1tg" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:NumberOfBatteriesPurchased" scale="0" id="Narr_N58XwCoBHk65ipj65GCnfg">33</ix:nonFraction> batteries under the agreement and had made advance payments relating to an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_jxoTQ30H-Ee41XEeUfi1tg" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:NumberOfBatteriesCommittedToBePurchasedDepositsMade" scale="0" id="Narr_rzDyFistM0GDrJBHsBAniA">63</ix:nonFraction> batteries. <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_jxoTQ30H-Ee41XEeUfi1tg" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:NumberOfBatteryUnitsInTransit" scale="0" id="Narr_sOwSgyOst0aFlTQRPC-04w">11</ix:nonFraction> of which are currently in transit.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On May 20, 2026, Neogy entered into liquidation proceedings in France. As a result of these proceedings and management&#8217;s assessment of the recoverability of the related deposits and the supplier&#8217;s ability to fulfill its contractual obligations, the Company recorded an impairment charge of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_3_1_2026_To_5_31_2026_HRfrjIJ0P0K6ZjEBCcZDuw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:AdvancesToSuppliersWriteDown" scale="0" id="Narr_l4sYcfQzfEGcbMHGaHdpUQ">1,092,925</ix:nonFraction>, which has been recognized in office and general expense during the three-month period ended May 31, 2026. <i style="font-style:italic;">[note 7]</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Given the commencement of the liquidation proceedings, the Company no longer considers the remaining purchase commitments under the supply agreement to represent enforceable future purchase obligations. Accordingly, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_DJ_Gbs_XZ0-yoXCWW_X2kQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="ifrs-full:ContractualCapitalCommitments" scale="0" id="Narr_aCQm89x2cUmS5rHl_oxY8g">no</ix:nonFraction> minimum purchase commitment has been disclosed as at May 31, 2026. The Company continues to monitor the liquidation proceedings and will pursue available legal remedies to maximize any potential recovery of amounts previously advanced.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">32</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;">Vision Marine Technologies Inc.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes to the condensed interim consolidated financial statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">(Unaudited)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">May 31, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="_a781143b_8850_4170_98c2_d3c2bd18cfe7"></a><a id="Tc_U1g9Qwwdm06yVSP04Z7dRA_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_nNMaemJvA0Sl5Hn3gA8-EQ_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_amZWyX4aG0mL9HnSjNKELg_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_H6ih880wK0uHJ76BTrQ80A_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_jKgAIcXGb0WWMH7xh5PFgA_5_0"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_ob40TqhLrEi2ItaLel-a4Q_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Future lease commitment</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">In October 2021, EB Rental FL Corp. has entered into lease arrangement for premises, which have not commenced yet and therefore related right-of-use asset and lease liability are not recorded as at May 31, 2026. The lease offers EB Rental FL Corp. a termination clause in case certain contractual requirements are not met by the lessor at the lease commencement date.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" name="vmar:IfrsDisclosureOfUndiscountedLeaseCommitmentsTableTextBlock" id="Tb_exFOJXabhkaIgcwTkvgBMA" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Company&#8217;s undiscounted lease commitments related to this lease are as follows as at May 31, 2026:</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:86.53%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.7%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:10.75%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:86.53%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.7%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">&#160;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;&#160;&#8203;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:10.75%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">$</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:86.53%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">2026</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.7%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:10.75%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_MaturityAxis_ifrs-full_NotLaterThanOneYearMember_bXhYPwEqBk6vwH6qDA0CDQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:GrossLeaseLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_HUCUSlSeLUeVImFozG6R6Q_2_2">30,000</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:86.53%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">2027</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.7%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:10.75%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_MaturityAxis_ifrs-full_LaterThanOneYearAndNotLaterThanTwoYearsMember_gf4EqvZMGECWKxLN67g2Pg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:GrossLeaseLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_SO6bbGwtmkmbNyMnKgHNaA_3_2">120,600</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:86.53%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">2028</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.7%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:10.75%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_MaturityAxis_ifrs-full_LaterThanTwoYearsAndNotLaterThanThreeYearsMember_SE0G_PU1U062rpHh5wMZXQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:GrossLeaseLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_DG1TILxMFk6UnHckW-Jt8g_4_2">123,012</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:86.53%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">2029 and thereafter</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.7%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:10.75%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.6pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2026_ifrs-full_MaturityAxis_vmar_LaterThanThreeYearsAndThereafterMember_Q6dGt4zmqE2JFS7l-Kbs2Q" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:GrossLeaseLiabilities" scale="0" id="Tc_NCHvi9jOCk6kp4e3n1nQ6g_5_2">350,868</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_1_2025_To_5_31_2026_HTBmuVpRt0andh7knIPPbQ" name="ifrs-full:DisclosureOfEventsAfterReportingPeriodExplanatory" id="Tb_FE1gRlY6HUuqpkKWVFjAzw" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">26. Subsequent events</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During the months of June and July 2026, the Company issued <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_PSKhk4L0BEuBjbMNWXfihw" contextRef="Duration_6_1_2026_To_7_31_2026_ifrs-full_NonadjustingEventsAfterReportingPeriodAxis_ifrs-full_MajorOrdinaryShareTransactionsMember_vmar_IfrsSaleOfStockAxis_vmar_AtMarketOfferingMember_8oxYzb-nyEKsfs83BYnCCw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsStockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesIssuedForServices" scale="0" id="Narr_CrCeK52caEC6AksQYn-CAA">1,871,347</ix:nonFraction> Voting Common Shares as part of an &#8220;at the market&#8221; placement offering for total gross proceeds of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="As_Of_7_31_2026_ifrs-full_NonadjustingEventsAfterReportingPeriodAxis_ifrs-full_MajorOrdinaryShareTransactionsMember_vmar_IfrsSaleOfStockAxis_vmar_AtMarketOfferingMember_7PylibOJgkOGnUGBRF-3sg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:ProceedsFromCapitalRaiseOfGrossReceivableFromPlacementAgent" scale="0" id="Narr_MqsQCv3HsECd3DpQMaktLQ">4,791,043</ix:nonFraction> less transaction costs of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_8tOzrXACyEyiIY7tlUEziA" contextRef="Duration_6_1_2026_To_7_31_2026_ifrs-full_NonadjustingEventsAfterReportingPeriodAxis_ifrs-full_MajorOrdinaryShareTransactionsMember_vmar_IfrsSaleOfStockAxis_vmar_AtMarketOfferingMember_8oxYzb-nyEKsfs83BYnCCw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:TransactionCostNetRelatedToIssuanceOfStock" scale="0" id="Narr_k0jYY8oBnk2o2lpvR0nw6w">201,299</ix:nonFraction>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On June 17, 2026, the Company implemented a reverse stock split, consolidating every <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_ifrs-full_NonadjustingEventsAfterReportingPeriodAxis_ifrs-full_MajorOrdinaryShareTransactionsMember_33nTLXtQf0S5RvDOIoQTLg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsStockholdersEquityNoteStockSplitConversionRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_DzT1yPJ8U0y6VwMwmPxMJw">10</ix:nonFraction> Voting Common shares into <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_xMlTUlsctESFATzoIj6QFg" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_ifrs-full_NonadjustingEventsAfterReportingPeriodAxis_ifrs-full_MajorOrdinaryShareTransactionsMember_33nTLXtQf0S5RvDOIoQTLg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:NumberOfReverseStockSplits" scale="0" id="Narr_OBdEI8r5DU2EYe95sONbnA">1</ix:nonFraction> Voting Common Share. As a result of the round up feature for fractional shares, the Company issued an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_PSKhk4L0BEuBjbMNWXfihw" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_ifrs-full_NonadjustingEventsAfterReportingPeriodAxis_ifrs-full_MajorOrdinaryShareTransactionsMember_33nTLXtQf0S5RvDOIoQTLg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="vmar:IfrsStockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesReverseStockSplits" scale="0" id="Narr_u82DoW7mik-zwHM_Gg6m8g">48,468</ix:nonFraction> Voting Common Shares.</p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="display:none;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';line-height:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">33</p></div></div>
